+## Rotating the password
+
+To change the `password` without signing everyone out, move the old one to `extraUnsealPasswords`:
+
+```js
+const session = await useSession(event, {
+  password: process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD,
+  extraUnsealPasswords: [process.env.OLD_SESSION_PASSWORD],
+});
+```
+
+Extra passwords only open sessions: sealing always uses `password`, and cookie sessions opened with an old one are resealed with the current one. Keep the list short, since every failed attempt costs PBKDF2 work, and only keep passwords you still trust. Sessions read from the header are not resealed, so they depend on the old password until they expire.
+
 ## Get Data from a Session
 
 To get data from a session, we will still use `useSession`. Under the hood, it will use `getSession` to get the session.
